Title: "Builtin Clause Commands"
Id: "b15bc21c-fa69-436a-8c94-53f29b6cdd07"

Text: "The formulation language provides builtin **command** forms that can be used
inline wherever a statement is expected. Builtin commands start with two
backslashes, and their arguments are separated by semicolons so an individual
argument may contain commas.

```mlg-fragment
\\not{P}
\\and{P; Q}
\\allOf{P; Q}
\\or{P; Q}
\\anyOf{P; Q}
\\oneOf{P; Q}
\\exists{x, y is \real; n is \natural}:suchThat{x * n > y}
\\existsUnique{x is \real}
\\forAll{x is \set}:where{x != y}:then{x is? \set}
\\if{P}:then{Q}
\\have{P}:iff{Q}
\\let{f is \function}:where{P}:then{Q}
\\piecewise:if{x = 0}:then{y = 0}:else{y = 1}
```

They use the same clause scoping rules: the
head arguments of `\\exists`, `\\existsUnique`, `\\forAll`, and `\\let`
introduce bindings in a child context, and `\\piecewise`'s `:else{...}` is
checked in the outer context.

The accepted tails are fixed per command:

- `\\exists` and `\\existsUnique` take an optional `:suchThat{...}`
- `\\forAll` (also spelled `\\forall`) and `\\let` take an optional
  `:where{...}` and a required `:then{...}`
- `\\if` takes `:then{...}`
- `\\have` requires `:iff{...}`
- `\\piecewise` takes `:if{...}`, a required `:then{...}`, and an optional
  `:else{...}`
- `\\not`, `\\and`, `\\allOf`, `\\or`, `\\anyOf`, and `\\oneOf` take no tails,
  and `\\not` expects exactly one clause

Wrong arity, a missing required tail, an unrecognized tail name, or an unknown
builtin clause command is reported as an error."
Id: "5267f2aa-8e87-45be-8219-e72918abb9b6"
